.TH "GLESHA-ARCHIVE" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-archive \- create a standalone encrypted archive
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha archive\fR PATH... [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Write an encrypted, compressed tar archive of PATH without registering a set. The output file must not exist.
.PP
The output is an OpenPGP message holding a compressed tar archive, so gpg and tar can also read it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-output FILE
Write to FILE (default: PREFIX\-TIME.tar.EXT.gpg in the current directory).
.SS Archive options
.TP
.B \-\-storage\-class CLASS
Ignored.
.TP
.B \-\-compression FORMAT
Compression: xz, gzip, or bzip2 (default: xz).
.TP
.B \-\-compression\-level N
Compression level, 1 to 9 (default: 6).
.TP
.B \-\-prefix PREFIX
Name prefix: glesha or encb (default: glesha).
.TP
.B \-\-archive\-mode MODE
Buffering: auto, memory, or stream (default: auto). With memory, the encrypted archive is held in memory and the command fails if it does not fit. With stream, it is written to a temporary file. With auto, it starts in memory and moves to a file when needed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the archive passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). A trailing newline is ignored. Without this option, the passphrase is read from a hidden prompt.
.SS Performance options
.TP
.B \-\-memory\-max SIZE
Memory limit (default: half of available memory, or 128MiB). SIZE takes a unit such as MiB or GiB and must be at least 48MiB. On Linux, the default is half of the available memory. On other systems, or if the available memory cannot be read, the default is 128MiB.
.TP
.B \-j, \-\-jobs, \-\-transfer\-workers N
Run up to N transfers at once (default: 4). The memory limit may lower the effective number.
.TP
.B \-\-hash\-workers N
Hash up to N files at once (default: 4).
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha archive ~/Documents
glesha archive ~/Documents \-\-output documents.tar.xz.gpg
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-decrypt (1),
.BR glesha\-extract (1)
